		<label>Type 86</label>
		<description>Caliber: 7.62x39mm. 30-round detachable mag. Select-Fire.
		
The Type 86 is a Chinese bullpup assault rifle based on the Type 56 Kalashnikov rifle. It is one of several bullpup configuration weapons that were tested by the PLA in the 1980s and was developed off of earlier rifles known as the WTC1 and WTC2. The Type 86 was most successful was a semi-auto locked civilian export weapon (the Type 86S) sold abroad, with about 2000 rifles being imported into the United States, but the select-fire military version seen here is a mythical variant that may or may not have actually been produced.</description>
